\f1\fs22 The High Elvis had forbid direct contact with the infected, lest the contagion escape. To stop Christianity creeping into their brains, all but a few select Elvi were ordered to wear ear-plugs when within ear-shot and even then the exposure was kept to a minimum. Notwithstanding the danger these Christians represented, The High Elvis was most reluctant to beat or torture one of their own but, as it turned out, the Epileptic Elvi were proud of what they had done, freely admitting to seditious acts against science and reason. The Dawkins wept.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>* * *\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They present very calm, great Sages, but when met with rational argument, they become wild eyed and agitated. Much to our shame, we had to resort to chaining them to their beds. They are through here, the four rooms immediately to the right. Beware, there is something godly happening here.\'94 Security Supervisor Elvis was genuinely frightened of the process of non-thinking called religion. His genome was susceptible to this meme and he did not fancy the prospects of losing his curiosity or his individualism. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It does not matter what you do to our flesh.\'94 Christian Elvis No 1 was adamant no one could change his mind about the Jesus. \'93We will be born again in the house of the lord. Jesus is the way the truth and the light. Praise him!\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You have not been born of water.\'94 Kleo was well versed in Christian fiction.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I have been baptised.\'94 Christian Elvis 1 quickly countered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Being born of woman is being born of water. You are a clone. You are born of syringe and petri-dish.\'94 Kleo heaped scorn upon ridicule. \'93You have no soul.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You lie. I have a soul.\'94 He hissed as his eyes popped and arteries in his forehead bulged and throbbed. \'93I have faith in the ancient scriptures.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your scripture has too many lies and inconsistencies to be regarded as anything but fantasy.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The scriptures are the word of god and therefore the truth. The life of Jesus of is no fantasy.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is an historical fact that the Gospels were scribed by those who almost certainly never met Jesus personally and were all devoutly convinced that his life must fulfill Old Testament prophecies. So sayeth the Dawkins.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are the stories of witnesses to my Lord Jesus and his miracles.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They were written decades after his death, are glaringly contradictory and simply implausible.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Jesus gave his life for all our sins.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Jesus knew dad was going to revive him. In those circumstances, dying is no sacrifice at all. He was sent on a suicide mission for no good reason.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You insult the Lord with your blasphemy.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I cannot insult something that does not exist.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your Evolution is nothing but a theory and your Dawkins was not an intellectual, but a failed celebrity.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The elegance of Darwinian Theory, has withstood punctilious examination for nearly two centuries, with no credible threat emerging. As science has advanced, Darwin has been proven correct, over and over again. The existence of God has been considered by the brightest minds for millennia, with no reliable evidence surfacing. Other than blind faith, there is no reason to believe in God.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What about Thomas Aquinas?\'94 Christian Elvis 1 was impressed with the logical progression of Aquinas and was unable to fault him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The Chronicles of the Dawkins tested Aquinas 
\f2\i reductio ad absurdium 
\f1\i0 and made him look a fool. Praise be to his wisdom.\'94 Kleo immediately countered. \'93In the absence of any evidence and in the same manner we reject Santa Claus, we must adopt the default position that God does not exist. We are then left with the explanations offered up by science, that time and space started with a single event and the expansion of the universe has unfolded under the influence of natural forces, one being evolution. If evidence of God\'92s existence does come to light, then I would reassess my position on the matter. This is the way of science, this is the way of the Dawkins\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Hartle-Hawking requires no single event.\'94 He was struggling now. He had read something about it recently, but had not really taken it all in.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Whether the Universe started with a single event or simply exists is another issue. Neither theory lend credence to god. In fact, Hartle-Hawking leaves no room for the existence of god. If you want to keep up with me you had better do some more homework, young Elvis.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I just need my faith. Praise be to Jesus. Pledge Now.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Clinging to faith is a rebuke of our natural curiosity, a rejection of reasoned thinking. Why would a God give us such a large brain and then ask us not to use it?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93God gave us such a brain so we could worship him.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He created the universe and then waited 14 billion years to be worshipped? The god described in your Bible is, in the words of the great one, \'91
\f2\i the most unpleasant character in all of fiction \'96 jealous and proud of it, vindictive, unjust, unforgiving, racist, an ethnic cleanser urging his people to acts of genocide.\'92 
\f1\i0 He asked Abraham to serve up his son to him as a burnt offering. In the name of the Dawkins, does that sound like the request of a moral god?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He is the truth from which all morality flows. I am in no position to judge the lord and neither are you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Then I shall speak of the characters mentioned in your scriptures. Moses brought the Ten Commandments down from the mountain and if my memory serves me correctly, one of those commandments was \'91Thou shall not kill\'92. The book of Numbers sees Moses displaying wanton disregard for the inscriptions carved upon those tablets. He became very angry at the merciful restraint of the Israelites towards the Midianite people and ordered all the men and the older women be put to death. He said \'91but all the women children that have not known a man by laying with him, keep for yourselves.\'92 Genocide and paedophilia does not a moral tale make.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93One example.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What of the man who was confronted, at his doorstep, by a mob demanding he give up his male guest for rape? He said, \'91Behold here is my daughter, a maiden, and his concubine. Them I will bring out now and humble ye them and do with them what seemeth good unto you, but unto him do not so vile a thing.\'92 It\'92s okay to rape a woman, but not a man? How can giving up your own child for rape be morally justifiable on any grounds? There are many stories your bible that could never be mistaken for moral tales.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I love Jesus of the New Testament.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>- - - \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo, Solo and Chilo sat before The High Elvis and his nervous cabinet in the committee room. They were hopeful of good news from the enlightened ones, but they looked somber and caught no-one in the eye.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are all devout, have no sense of humour and follow neither logic nor reason. This infection has blocked their capacity to comprehend simple scientific facts. They are, for want of a better term, possessed by the Jesus and we have no alternative but to excise this meme and purge them of faith.\'94 Kleo had not seen faith manifest itself with such fervor and doubted anything, at least in the short term, was going to work. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How is that achieved? I do not want them to come to harm.\'94 The High Elvis had led a long cabinet session on Elvi detention policy and had concluded, under no circumstances, could the \'91Fucked-up-five\'92 be deliberately harmed, beaten or tortured. That sort of thing was contrary to any civilised moral code and completely beneath their dignity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Of course, High Elvis. I think we should start off by playing rock and roll music, twenty four hours a day. Then science documentaries, interspersed with de-programming sessions where my colleagues and I will challenge their beliefs with rational argument and scientific truth. If this fails we may have to call on ancient methods to rid them of evil.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I authorise you and your colleagues to commence the rock n\'92 roll therapy and the follow up documentary and counselling sessions, wise one.\'94 The High Elvis felt like he was getting used to this leadership thing. \'93I want regular reports. We will reassess as each day goes by.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Thank you, High Elvis. What if the therapy fails?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We will continue to try. We have no legal authority to hold them but they represent an unacceptable threat to Elvi culture and we cannot afford to let them go. If we exile them, into the general PTD population, the Directory of Moral Observance will have them killed the moment they out themselves as Christian. I cannot allow that. They must be kept away from the rest of us until they are rendered safe.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93That could be many years, High Elvis.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I fear that to be true, wise one, but I cannot allow my Elvi to be harmed, let alone killed. They are not being held to punish, but to protect.\'94 High Elvis did not think that sitting in the big chair would be so fraught with moral predicaments. When he entered the race for the top job, he reasoned it would be a largely ceremonial position where he would make a few speeches, maybe kiss a few babies and shake some hands. The position itself had no authority within the Primary Trade Dominion, making the detention of five Elvis clones highly illegal. If discovered, he and his leadership team would most certainly be detained by the PTD. \'93I am not satisfied it is morally unjustifiable to kill an Elvis or by omission allow an Elvis to die.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You will be a great leader, High Elvis.\'94 Kleo and his crew were impressed. This Elvis had done some serious thinking and seemed to have a finely tuned moral compass which he confidently applied to the ever changing circumstance of politics. A skill mostly unknown in the Primary Trade Dominion, where moral compasses were very rare indeed.
